[finding] f-017 Verbatim-cited (cite() succeeded, references.bib in run dir): Planck 2018 Omega_c h^2 = 0.120 +/- 0.001 (1807.06209 abstract); thermal higgsino mass ~1.2 TeV wi
**Finding:** Verbatim-cited (cite() succeeded, references.bib in run dir): Planck 2018 Omega_c h^2 = 0.120 +/- 0.001 (1807.06209 abstract); thermal higgsino mass ~1.2 TeV with coannihilation + Sommerfeld (2410.15733), m ~1.08 TeV 'cosmologically preferred' (2609.02775), ~1.1 TeV (2609.02608, with delta ~377 keV for LZ event), upper end 1150 GeV for higgsino-like thermal DM (2403.19598); solar-capture IceCube bound delta > 566 keV at m=1.08 TeV (2609.02775). The 1.08-1.2 TeV spread is not resolved from abstracts: 2410.15733 explicitly includes Sommerfeld+coannihilation; the others do not state their treatment in the abstract, so attributing the spread to bound-state formation/NLO/Planck input remains unverified (likely ~10% theory systematics; consensus band 1.08-1.2 TeV, central ~1.1 TeV).
