**Finding:** At 1.1 TeV the LZ 4.2 t-yr (arXiv:2410.17036, Fig. 5, from HEPData record 155182 table t1) observed 90% CL SI limit is about 3.3e-47 cm^2 and the median sensitivity is about 7.5e-47 cm^2. These were scaled linearly from the 1008 GeV HEPData values (observed 3.056e-47, median 6.834e-47 cm^2; above 1 TeV the limit scales as m^0.985). XENONnT 3.1 t-yr (arXiv:2502.18005) states in its text that above 200 GeV the limit is 3.7e-46 cm^2 x (M/1 TeV), which gives about 4.1e-46 cm^2 at 1.1 TeV.
