[finding] f-020 Change from first runs to current results at 1.1 TeV: XENONnT went from 6.08e-47 x (M/100 GeV) cm^2 (arXiv:2303.14729, about 6.7e-46 cm^2 at 1.1 TeV, with a con
**Finding:** Change from first runs to current results at 1.1 TeV: XENONnT went from 6.08e-47 x (M/100 GeV) cm^2 (arXiv:2303.14729, about 6.7e-46 cm^2 at 1.1 TeV, with a conservative median power constraint) to 3.7e-46 x (M/1 TeV) cm^2 (arXiv:2502.18005, about 4.1e-46 cm^2), an improvement of about 1.6x. For LZ, the text gives only the minimum limits, 9.2e-48 cm^2 at 36 GeV for the first run (2207.03764) and 2.2e-48 cm^2 at 40 GeV for 4.2 t-yr (2410.17036), an improvement of about 4.2x at the minimum. The first-run LZ value at 1 TeV was not obtained.
