[finding] f-022 At 1.1 TeV the pure thermal higgsino (sigma_SI <~ 1e-48 cm^2) lies at least about 33x below the LZ 4.2 t-yr observed limit (about 3.3e-47 cm^2), at least about 
**Finding:** At 1.1 TeV the pure thermal higgsino (sigma_SI <~ 1e-48 cm^2) lies at least about 33x below the LZ 4.2 t-yr observed limit (about 3.3e-47 cm^2), at least about 75x below the LZ median sensitivity, and at least about 400x below the XENONnT 3.1 t-yr limit (about 4.1e-46 cm^2). It is also at least about 5.5x below the xenon SI neutrino floor (O'Hare 2109.03116 data file Xe_SI.txt: 5.0e-48 cm^2 at 1 TeV, about 5.5e-48 cm^2 at 1.1 TeV by linear scaling), so it sits inside the neutrino fog. The LZ limit itself is only about 6x above the floor at 1 TeV.
