[tool] d-09 post_finding {"claim": "The tree-level neutral higgsino splitting is delta0 ~ m_Z^2 (s_W^2/M1 + c_W^2/M2) for M_i >> |mu|, with tan beta cancelling at O(1/M) (Nagata and Shi
[finding] f-027 The tree-level neutral higgsino splitting is delta0 ~ m_Z^2 (s_W^2/M1 + c_W^2/M2) for M_i >> |mu|, with tan beta cancelling at O(1/M) (Nagata and Shirai, arXiv:
**Finding:** The tree-level neutral higgsino splitting is delta0 ~ m_Z^2 (s_W^2/M1 + c_W^2/M2) for M_i >> |mu|, with tan beta cancelling at O(1/M) (Nagata and Shirai, arXiv:1410.4549, Eqs. 15 and 34). For M1 = M2 = M (m_Z^2 = 8315 GeV^2), the required gaugino mass is M = 2.38e7 GeV at delta = 350 keV, 2.25e7 GeV at 370 keV, 2.16e7 GeV at 385 keV and 1.47e7 GeV at 566 keV. The xenon-accessible window of about 345-385 keV therefore needs gauginos at about 2.2-2.4 x 10^4 TeV, not 10-30 TeV. The solar bound (delta > 566 keV) requires M < 1.5 x 10^4 TeV. With wino exchange only (delta0 = m_W^2/M2) these values are about 22% lower. RG running of the dimension-5 operators (1410.4549, Eq. 35, Fig. 6) and on-shell one-loop mass corrections (2609.09830, Eqs. 19-20) change the splitting multiplicatively by tens of percent. The exact percentage was not extracted.
[tool] tc-261022_1-w2-d-09-85 -> ok: Recorded finding f-027.
[tool] d-09 post_finding {"claim": "In the higgsino limit, the tree-level Higgs-exchange coupling is f_q ~ -(g^2/8m_h^2)[1/(M2-|mu|) + tan^2 theta_W/(M1-|mu|)](1 + sgn(mu) sin 2beta) (a
[finding] f-028 In the higgsino limit, the tree-level Higgs-exchange coupling is f_q ~ -(g^2/8m_h^2)[1/(M2-|mu|) + tan^2 theta_W/(M1-|mu|)](1 + sgn(mu) sin 2beta) (arXiv:2606.3
**Finding:** In the higgsino limit, the tree-level Higgs-exchange coupling is f_q ~ -(g^2/8m_h^2)[1/(M2-|mu|) + tan^2 theta_W/(M1-|mu|)](1 + sgn(mu) sin 2beta) (arXiv:2606.31013, Eqs. 30-33; arXiv:1410.4549, Eqs. 46-49). This gives roughly sigma_SI ~ 5e-46 cm^2 (1 TeV/M)^2 (1 + sgn mu sin2beta)^2 for M1 = M2 = M; my order-of-magnitude check agrees to within a factor of about 3. With the large-tan-beta factor of about 1, sigma_SI reaches the LZ 4.2 t-yr limit of about 3.3e-47 cm^2 at 1.1 TeV (f-019) for M of about 4 TeV, or about 0.7 TeV with the 1e-45 placeholder. At M = 4 TeV the splitting is m_Z^2/M, about 2 GeV, so inelastic scattering is closed. In the inelastic window (M ~ 2.3e4 TeV) sigma_SI is about 1e-54 cm^2, 7-8 orders below LZ and far below the neutrino floor. The Higgs-exchange elastic signal and the inelastic xenon signal are therefore mutually exclusive, which answers q-11.
